Are you discouraged by never getting below the first few levels of
NH3.0?  Here's a line of play that routinely gets me down to the
deeper levels.

It is comprised of several tricks that I pulled from this newsgroup,
and so this is only to give new players an organized plan of attack.



Play a Valkyrie, and if you want restart new games until you get
strength 18/03 or better.

Make your first priority to get to experience level 5, and notice
where the fountains are as you go.  I usually go straight down to
levels 3 and 4 where you can gain experience levels quickly.  
Be sure to kill acid blobs and green molds by kicking them, and not
by using your long sword.

You start with a food ration as a Valkyrie, and so it is not usually
necessary to use prayer to take care of your stomach.  What you can
do is to stand on a staircase and let a rat or jackal bite you
until your hit points are around 7 or so.  Then, go down the stairs
and kick a wall until your hit points are less than 5 and pray.
The gods will usually give you more hit points.  You can do this
a several times on the first five levels, with the first time occuring
on any turn after 300.

When you are at exp. level 5 go to a fountain on the highest level
where one appears.  Now, you're ready to dip your long sword
until it gets blessed.  If your sword gets rusted a couple of
times, your desire to continue this game will of course be
decreased.  I have been known to quit if this happens to me.
Usually it doesn't get rusted twice, though.  After you have a
blessed +1 long sword named Excalibur it is relatively easy to
kill ants, rothes, and orcs.

Once you find these tougher monsters try to fight them standing on
a stair case or in a hallway where you have room to run away to a
staircase.  After you get used to fighting this way, you start getting
a lot farther down in the dungeon.

Don't quaff from fountains hoping to get a wish, this very rarely
happens.  You can use the fountains to create potions of water, to
remove curses, and to create blank scrolls by dipping the appropriate
object into the fountain.  These uses of a fountain will give you
more advantage in the long run than will trying for a wish.

Since I save fountains for these purposes I'm not too inhibited about
trying on good armor that I find.  (Avoid any boot that is not called
a hard shoe.  Cursed levitation boots will almost surely ruin your game.)
If you get a piece of cursed armor that has negative enchantments you
can remove the curse by dipping it in the fountains.


